#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203797 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d6226fdb-ee73-5a78-87d5-9d6a988a9eb4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Equation With No Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "fd07ad0f-548a-5569-84de-d658a88c4b9c" :question/math-academy-id "e-17087" :question/problem "Which of the following equations has no solutions?\n\n1. $4z + 3 = 4z + 9$\n2. $2z - 5 = z + 1$\n3. $3z - 2 = 3z - 2$" :question/worked-solution "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n$4z + 3|= 4z + 9; 4z + 3 - 4z|= 4z + 9 - 4z; 3|= 9$.\nThis equation is false for all values of $z$. Therefore, the equation $4z + 3 = 4z + 9$ has no solutions.\n- For the second equation, we have\n$2z - 5|= z + 1; 2z - 5 - z + 5|= z + 1 - z + 5; z|= 6$.\nTherefore, the equation $2z - 5 = z + 1$ has the unique solution $z = 6$.\n- For the third equation, we have\n$3z - 2|= 3z - 2; 3z - 2 - 3z|= 3z - 2 - 3z; - 2|=-2$.\nThis equation is true for all values of $z$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203798 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/id #uuid "cba9196c-fdc3-594d-a1ad-948cf75bd366" :question/math-academy-id "e-17213" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y$, given by\n$4(r - 2)y = -8$\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r$?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n$ax = b$\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and\n\n$$\nb\\neq 0\n$$\n\nIf $a = 0$, then the equation has no solution.\n\nNotice that this equation is in the form $ay = b$. In this case,\n\n$$\na = 4(r - 2), \\qquad b = -8\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n4(r - 2) = 0\n$$\n\nSolving this for $r$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4(r - 2) &= 0 \\\\\n(4(r - 2))/(4) &= \\frac{0}{4} \\\\\nr - 2 &= 0 \\\\\nr &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203799 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d63847ef-6360-50b5-b585-9084140b2d67" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Variables and Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/id #uuid "36eadc0b-c2b0-5f84-8f39-2b8399932edb" :question/math-academy-id "e-17214" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x$, given by\n$2nx + 7 = -4x + 5$\nwhere $n$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $n$?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n$ax = b$\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and\n\n$$\nb\\neq 0\n$$\n\nIf $a = 0$, then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation in the form $ax = b$.\n\nWe start by adding $4x$ to both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2nx + 7 &= -4x + 5 \\\\\n2nx + 4x + 7 &= -4x + 5 + 4x \\\\\n2nx + 4x + 7 &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we subtract $7$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2nx + 4x + 7 &= 5 \\\\\n2nx + 4x + 7 - 7 &= 5 - 7 \\\\\n2nx + 4x &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor $x$ on the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n(2n + 4)x = -2\n$$\n\nNotice that this equation is now in the form $ax = b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{(2n + 4)}_{a}x = \\underbrace{-2}_{b}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n\n$$\n2n + 4= 0\n$$\n\nSolving this for $n$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2n + 4 &= 0 \\\\\n2n + 4 - 4 &= 0 - 4 \\\\\n2n &= -4 \\\\\n\\frac{2n}{2} &= \\frac{-4}{2} \\\\\nn &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186203820 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/id #uuid "5ee14499-89b0-59a3-9f13-b0a00c0e518d" :question/math-academy-id "e-18853" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $z$, given by\n$(r - 9)z + 2 = -1$\nwhere $r$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $r$?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have an equation of the form\n$ax = b$\nwhere $a$ and $b$ are constants, and\n\n$$\nb\\neq 0\n$$\n\nIf $a = 0$, then the equation has no solution.\n\nFirst, let's write our equation in the form $az = b{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(r - 9)z + 2 &= -1 \\\\\n(r - 9)z + 2 - 2 &= -1 - 2 \\\\\n(r - 9)_(⏟)_(a)z &= -3_(⏟)_(b)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has no solution if\n$r - 9 = 0$.\n\nSolving this for $r$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr - 9 &= 0 \\\\\nr &= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204539 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba644b27-7245-5b7b-8cd6-2493836a7d03" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter - Constants on Both Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1afe64ee-6a95-55d0-ae94-eebb04a6359d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1afe64ee-6a95-55d0-ae94-eebb04a6359d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232435} :answer-field/id #uuid "871f23cd-6756-596d-8c73-99acd164790c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203438}] :question/id #uuid "38670cb7-04d7-5bd3-bbc0-32b596369870" :question/math-academy-id "q-287667" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $x$, given by\n$2(p - 4)x + 2 = 5$\nwhere $p$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $p$?$p =$\n{{field-1}}\n\n---\n\n<a id=\"solving-for-an-unknown-parameter-variables-and-constants-on-both-sides\"></a>"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204544 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e7426e-553d-5f20-811f-15f3a5ea0056" :knowledge-point/title "Solving For an Unknown Parameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d0b2e78a-6e20-549c-bc9b-892664180c32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203459} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d04615-1d41-5a45-ba9b-8ba79bb5ff41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203460} {:answer/id #uuid "fb9e3819-10ff-5567-a85b-bddce1db025c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203461} {:answer/id #uuid "2e74dea8-50dc-55e4-b514-bbcd47a4907c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203462} {:answer/id #uuid "55315068-5d60-51ae-a190-c7d4dbfb8e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9d04615-1d41-5a45-ba9b-8ba79bb5ff41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203460} :answer-field/id #uuid "4594c658-f6ef-5788-bb0b-f1d8af9ae065" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203458}] :question/id #uuid "328a41df-8074-5d3e-9600-d58da9a2fa99" :question/math-academy-id "q-288593" :question/problem "Consider the equation in the variable $y$, given by\n\n$(q - 1)y = 4$\nwhere $q$ is a constant. Given that this equation has no solution, what is the value of $q$?"}]}
